    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1027">

                <pb facs="1083" n="1073" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1073"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.0031 Tibet/5–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Henderson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-03T19:00:00-04:00">May 3, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>328. NY FR<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1027-f1"/> Bank has recd request Leader, Tibet
                    Trade Mission to sell some $US 400,000 of gold for air shipment vaults Hong Kong
                    [and] Shanghai Banking Corp., 31 Dalhousie Square, Calcutta, West Bengal. When
                    Trade Mission in US this Govt inclined to honor such request to Tibetan <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Govt but had misgivings re end use of
                    gold, that is in event premium sales Tibet or elsewhere involved. Pls ascertain
                    discreetly possible end uses and attitude of GoI auths such transaction if
                    approved here. Leader TTM states some dols to be released by GoI.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1027-f1" n="10" xml:id="d1027-f1-content">
                <p>Federal Reserve.</p>
            </note>
